[TITLE]
Storage / outfall fixture for the node-profile probe.
The initial depth of a storage unit can only be set by the parser: the C API's
swmm_node_set_initial_depth() writes the node's CURRENT depth, while
swmm_node_get_initial_depth() reads init_depth, so an in-memory fixture cannot
exercise the water surface. Hence this file.

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
INFILTRATION         HORTON
FLOW_ROUTING         DYNWAVE
START_DATE           01/01/2020
START_TIME           00:00:00
END_DATE             01/01/2020
END_TIME             06:00:00
REPORT_STEP          00:05:00
ROUTING_STEP         00:00:15

[JUNCTIONS]
;;Name  Elev   MaxDepth  InitDepth  SurDepth  Aponded
J1      106.0  8.0       0.0        0.0       0.0

[STORAGE]
;;Name  Elev   MaxDepth  InitDepth  Shape       A1/L  A2/W  A0/Z
POND    100.0  10.0      4.0        FUNCTIONAL  500   1.5   200

[OUTFALLS]
;;Name  Elev   Type   StageData  Gated
OF_FIX  90.0   FIXED  95.0       YES
OF_FREE 90.0   FREE              NO

[CONDUITS]
;;Name  From    To       Length  N      InOff  OutOff  InitFlow  MaxFlow
C1      J1      POND     300     0.013  0.0    0.0     0         0
C2      POND    OF_FIX   120     0.013  0.0    1.0     0         0
C3      J1      OF_FREE  200     0.013  0.0    0.0     0         0

[XSECTIONS]
;;Link  Shape     Geom1  Geom2  Geom3  Geom4  Barrels
C1      CIRCULAR  2.5    0      0      0      1
C2      CIRCULAR  3.0    0      0      0      1
C3      CIRCULAR  1.5    0      0      0      1

[COORDINATES]
;;Node  X      Y
J1      0      300
POND    300    300
OF_FIX  600    300
OF_FREE 300    0
